# Trivy allowlist (Step 3.3 / plan Step 22).
#
# Policy: CI fails on *fixable* HIGH/CRITICAL findings in the images we build
# (--ignore-unfixed handles the unfixable ones automatically). Anything listed
# here must carry a reason and an expiry date; when the date passes, the entry
# is treated as a failure — either fix it or consciously re-approve it.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-XXXX-YYYY  # <reason> — expires YYYY-MM-DD
#
# pyasn1 0.4.8 in the agent image. The fixes need pyasn1>=0.6, which breaks the
# pinned pysnmp 4.4.12; clearing them requires migrating the agent to a
# maintained pysnmp and re-running `make simulation`. Same deferral as the
# pip-audit --ignore-vuln entries in .github/workflows/ci.yml
# (PYSEC-2026-2263 / -3455 / -3456 / -3457).
CVE-2026-30922  # pyasn1 0.4.8, needs >=0.6.3 — expires 2026-10-31
CVE-2026-59884  # pyasn1 0.4.8, needs >=0.6.4 — expires 2026-10-31
CVE-2026-59885  # pyasn1 0.4.8, needs >=0.6.4 — expires 2026-10-31
CVE-2026-59886  # pyasn1 0.4.8, needs >=0.6.4 — expires 2026-10-31
